{"name":"Midnight Blue","hex":"#020035","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark blue color, almost black."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark blue color, almost black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight_blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight Blue (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight Blue is a sexually themed cable television program that aired on Manhattan Cable Television Channel J in New York City."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_Blue_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q16951968"},{"title":"Midnight Blue (Melissa Manchester song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Midnight Blue\" is a song by American singer and songwriter Melissa Manchester, written by herself alongside Carole Bayer Sager and produced by Vini Poncia with an executive production by Richard Perry. It was released in April 1975 as the first single from Manchester's third studio album, Melissa (1975)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/Midnight_Blue_-_Melissa_Manchester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_Blue_(Melissa_Manchester_song)","wikidata":"Q6842656"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https:/